message: "Please cite the relevant theorem paper and computational specification, and cite the underlying arithmetic sources separately."
type: software
title: "Polynomial presentations of the integers over the rationals"
authors:
  - name: "ℤℚ Diophantine Project contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
url: "https://github.com/JoseBrox/diophantine-z-q_improvements"
date-released: 2026-11-17
version: "2026.11.17-v56"
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Mathematical proofs and exact specifications for polynomial presentations
  of the integers over the rationals, under explicitly stated arithmetic
  premises. Established constructions use 25 variables with degree below
  2^53, or 195 variables with degree four. Fully specified constructions
  use 27 variables with degree below 2^57 and coefficient height below
  2^(2^70), or 257 quartic variables. Additional weak abc hypotheses give
  13 variables with degree below 2^26. Ordinary rational abc gives a
  71-variable quartic with 1187 monomials and coefficient height B^2+1
  for every permitted fixed odd B >= 81. All counts include the input.
  Sufficient parameters for the existence families remain ineffective.
  Supporting theorems include guarded finite-algebra encodings, elliptic
  height estimates, a single-cover soundness criterion, finite exceptional
  square-class menus and a degree-nine prepared pole block of coefficient
  height four. Uniform rational realization for the 21/9 targets remains
  unproved. The full independent audit of retained arithmetic foundations
  is not declared complete. Cite the project and this repository as
  specified in the README Contributors and citation subsection.
keywords:
  - Diophantine definitions
  - Hilbert's tenth problem
  - rational points
  - explicit polynomials
  - elliptic heights
  - finite algebraic elimination
  - number fields
